The function is already minimal, so this is a micro-change rather than a real speedup. It loads `profile` into a local once and marks the invalid path as unlikely. That gives the compiler a straight-line fast path, and behavior is unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    const Profile::MESG* const p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields), 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    return p->fields[profileIndex].num;
}
```